From: Ifran Ali <khanu.i.i.k.2000@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: rtw89: 8852c: move common code to rtw8852c_common.c

The RTL8192XB is a 2.4 GHz chip of the RTL8852C family. Realtek's driver
shares about half of the 8852C code with it: the MAC and BB glue, TX
power control, coex hooks and PPDU parsing. Calibration, channel and
bandwidth setup, efuse layout and power-on differ.

Move the shared part to a new rtw89_8852c_common module, the way
rtw8852b_common.c serves the RTL8852B and RTL8852BT. Exported functions
are reached through rtw8852cx_info. The code is moved as-is, with no
functional change.

Signed-off-by: Ifran Ali <khanu.i.i.k.2000@gmail.com>
